<title>GERMANY: Waigel-Bonn to meet EMU criteria in 97, beat in 98.</title>
<headline>Waigel-Bonn to meet EMU criteria in 97, beat in 98.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Tuesday Germany would meet the entry criteria for European economic and monetary union (EMU) in 1997, and beat the fiscal targets in 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;We will hold to the Maastricht criteria in 1997 and improve in 1998,&quot; Waigel said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
